WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.501
I want to do something that
matters.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:06.673
♪♪

00:00:07.758 --> 00:00:10.177
Emily, you're a poet.

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:12.054
You work so hard on your poems.

00:00:12.054 --> 00:00:14.056
You want every line to be
perfect.

00:00:14.056 --> 00:00:16.225
But I want the mess.

00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:18.560
I want you.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.479
♪♪

00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:22.397
Emily:
This is a very dark time.

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:23.607
Emily:
The violence.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:25.275
Emily:
The suffering.

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:26.485
♪♪

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:28.570
Emily:
That's what I want to heal,

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:29.988
with my poetry.

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:32.032
Words don't matter right now.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:32.991
♪♪

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:34.993
I have so much poetry in my
head.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.996
Emily:
With all this conflict, none of
it has been able to come out.

00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:40.749
This family is a joke.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:41.750
My marriage is a lie.

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:45.003
Civil war ruins everything.

00:00:45.212 --> 00:00:46.755
♪♪

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:48.882
This war just came out of
nowhere.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.510
I'm not sure about that. 
I think it was pretty clear we
were headed in a bad direction.

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:54.554
♪♪

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.515
You're really the only one brave
enough to face the truth.

00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:57.933
♪♪

00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.935
You're not trying to peddle some
false hope.

00:00:59.935 --> 00:01:01.561
What if hope is all we have?

00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:05.107
♪♪

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:07.734
My family is in complete chaos.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.112
Emily:
But nothing I do seems to be making
anything any better.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:12.030
♪♪

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.366
You think you're fighting for
something, but really 

00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:16.076
you're just running away.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:21.039
♪♪

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:23.458
To be a great poet, you have to
feel everything.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.044
Walt Whitman:
The pleasure, the pain,

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.879
the sunlight, the shade.

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.756
Yeah, he just takes it a little
bit too far.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.174
Yesssss!

00:01:31.258 --> 00:01:32.259
Death:
Come on, now.

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:35.429
Where do you get that fire from?

00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:37.556
♪♪

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.266
Emily:
I can't live without you.

00:01:39.266 --> 00:01:41.310
I can't breathe without you.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:44.354
♪♪

00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:45.981
I want to do something that
matters.

00:01:45.981 --> 00:01:51.194
♪♪

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:54.406
Don't worry, everyone.
Emily Dickinson is here to help.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:58.285
♪♪

00:01:58.285 --> 00:02:00.662
In the future, you're actually
famous.

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:03.290
Emily Dickinson was the original
sad girl.

